{"chunk_id": "b9358e14db23", "text": "After King Dasaratha\u2019s great sacrifice concludes, the gods return to heaven and the king returns to Ayodhya filled with hope for heirs. In an astrologically auspicious moment during the month of Chaitra, the divine plan unfolds: Vishnu incarnates as Rama, born to Queen Kaushalya. Bharata is born to Kaikeyi, and the twins Lakshmana and Shatrughna to Sumitra, each sharing a portion of Vishnu\u2019s glory. Celestial signs accompany their births\u2014gods shower flowers, heavenly music sounds, and the capital rejoices. The princes grow in wisdom, martial skill, and virtue, with Rama shining above all in truth and nobility. Lakshmana becomes inseparably devoted to him, while Bharata and Shatrughna form a similar bond. The chapter ends with the dramatic arrival of the powerful sage Vishwamitra at Dasaratha\u2019s court, foreshadowing the princes\u2019 first great adventure.\nAfter Dasaratha\u2019s sacrifice, Rama, Bharata, Lakshmana, and Shatrughna are born, grow in virtue and skill, and the sage Vishwamitra arrives at the court.\nThemes: divine birth, royal lineage, brotherly devotion, education of princes, arrival of sage", "vector": [0.019360069185495377, -0.02255542017519474, -0.019574882462620735, -0.01964201219379902, -0.017440173774957657, 0.018312852829694748, -0.01880960911512375, -0.013701075688004494, -0.029778525233268738, -0.014620746485888958, 0.011787892319262028, 0.006454475224018097, -0.014902688562870026, 0.026247529312968254, 0.0006142324418760836, 0.003388347802683711, 0.040921978652477264, -0.02259569801390171, 0.030073894187808037, 0.0014088746393099427, 0.01592305302619934, -0.02130681648850441, 0.005531448405236006, 0.030369263142347336, -0.017789246514439583, 0.006212810054421425, 0.016742030158638954, -0.021816998720169067, 0.013727927580475807, -0.019480902701616287, -0.009572627954185009, -0.0182188730686903, 0.009290684945881367, -0.012150390073657036, -0.022273479029536247, -0.0007249956834129989, -0